msgid "``serialize`` — Serialisation Infrastructure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Internal module — subject to change without notice.** Do not import "
"these functions directly. Use the public serialisation methods on "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` instead (``to_json``, "
"``from_json``, ``to_pickle``, ``from_pickle``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Private serialization infrastructure for ndict_tools."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This module is **not part of the public API**. It provides the low-level "
"helpers used by the serialization methods on ``_StackedDict`` "
"(``to_json``, ``from_json``, ``to_pickle``, ``from_pickle``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``_encode_key`` / ``_decode_key`` : JSON key encoding via type-tagged "
"string prefix"
msgstr ""

msgid "``NestedDictionaryEncoder``       : ``json.JSONEncoder`` subclass"
msgstr ""

msgid "``_make_decoder_hook``            : factory for ``object_pairs_hook``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``_pickle_dump`` / ``_pickle_load``: pickle helpers with SHA-256 "
"verification"
msgstr ""

msgid "Design decisions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**JSON key encoding** (design decision `#87 "
"<https://github.com/biface/ndt/issues/87>`_): JSON mandates string keys; "
"Python supports arbitrary hashable keys. Non-string keys are encoded as "
"``__type__:value`` tagged strings (e.g., ``__int__:42``, ``__tuple__:(1, "
"2)``). Decoding uses ``ast.literal_eval`` for safe reconstruction of "
"``tuple`` and ``frozenset`` values. Known limitation: string keys that "
"already start with a ``__type__:`` prefix are indistinguishable from "
"encoded keys."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**API placement** (design decision `#94 "
"<https://github.com/biface/ndt/issues/94>`_): Serialization methods "
"(``to_json``, ``from_json``, ``to_pickle``, ``from_pickle``) are defined "
"on ``_StackedDict`` and delegate to the private helpers below via lazy "
"imports. This creates an accepted import cycle between ``tools.py`` and "
"this module."
msgstr ""

msgid "Key encoding (DD-021)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Encode a ``_StackedDict`` key to a JSON-safe string."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JSON mandates string keys. This function maps any supported hashable "
"Python key to a unique, reversible string using a type-tagged prefix of "
"the form ``__type__:value`` (e.g., integer ``42`` → ``\"__int__:42\"``, "
"tuple ``(1, 2)`` → ``\"__tuple__:(1, 2)\"``). Plain string keys are "
"passed through unchanged. Known limitation: a string key that already "
"starts with a recognised prefix (e.g. ``\"__int__:42\"``) is "
"indistinguishable from an encoded integer key after a round-trip."
msgstr ""

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key to encode. Supported types: ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, "
"``bool``, flat ``tuple`` of scalars, flat ``frozenset`` of scalars."
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

msgid "A JSON-safe string representing the key."
msgstr ""

