msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``bool`` is tested before ``int`` because ``bool`` is a subclass of "
"``int``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``float`` values use ``repr()`` to preserve full precision."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``frozenset`` is unordered: element order in the encoded form is not "
"guaranteed. Round-trip preserves set equality, not element ordering."
msgstr ""

msgid "Decode an encoded JSON key back to its original Python type."
msgstr ""

msgid "Applies five sequential decoding rules in priority order:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``__bool__:`` prefix → ``bool`` (checked before ``int`` to avoid "
"misclassification)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``__int__:`` prefix → ``int``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``__float__:`` prefix → ``float``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``__frozenset__:`` prefix → ``frozenset`` (via ``ast.literal_eval``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``__tuple__:`` prefix → ``tuple`` (via ``ast.literal_eval``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "No recognised prefix → plain ``str`` (identity)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"No ``eval()`` is used. ``ast.literal_eval()`` is used only for flat "
"tuples of Python scalars, which are valid Python literals by definition."
msgstr ""

msgid "The encoded JSON key string produced by ``_encode_key``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The original Python key."
msgstr ""

msgid "Decoding rules (applied in order):"
msgstr ""

msgid "Starts with ``\\[`` → strip ``\\``, return as ``str``."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Starts with ``[frozenset{`` and ends with ``}]`` → parse inner CSV of "
"scalars, return as ``frozenset``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Starts with ``[(`` and ends with ``)]`` → ``ast.literal_eval()``, return "
"as ``tuple``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Starts with ``[`` and ends with ``]`` → infer scalar type "
"(``True``/``False`` → ``bool``; ``.`` or ``e`` → ``float``; else "
"``int``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Otherwise → return as ``str`` unchanged."
msgstr ""

